  "detail": "Thank you: the restart flow, the boot check and the docs all look right. One ordering problem remains, shown by an orchestrator probe with an injected deferred drain request. (1) `requestAdmin(client, clock, \"drain\")` is sent and is still pending. (2) SIGINT arrives, and `race` rejects at once. (3) The cleanup path sends `resume`, the restart exits non-zero and releases the lock. (4) The original drain request is then applied by the daemon, so it stays `draining: true` with nobody left to resume it. The interrupt test at test/restart.test.ts:167 applies the drain before emitting the signal, so it misses this order. Fix: keep the drain request's promise, and on an interrupt wait for it to settle (bounded by the existing request timeout) before deciding whether to resume, so a resume is never sent ahead of a drain still in flight. Deploy's own drain at line 694 and service install's at line 368 race the same way, so put the fix in one shared place that all three use rather than three copies (AGENTS.md: one guard, every path). Add a test with a drain request that resolves only after the interrupt: the final state is not draining, resume is sent after the drain applied, and no kickstart happens. Run it for restart and for deploy. It must fail without the fix. Run only the affected test files (test/restart.test.ts test/deploy.test.ts test/deploy-process.test.ts test/drain-http.test.ts test/service.test.ts), `bunx biome check` on the changed files and `bunx tsc --noEmit`. Never run the full suite in a factory run (AGENTS.md)."
